1790107586939358	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyoBA		item.comment	bn-1z09m	{"body":"Startup task-resolution pass landed in ws bn-1z09m (commits 98c3e07..8b14e41). recovery::resolve_tasks(store, cap) reads every task_ index entry, strictly decodes it as a campaign record (inverse of budget::publication_record; typed RecordDefect per cause), groups by task, and resolves each: SequenceGap / AmbiguousHead -> Failed; closed head -> Settled; bounded head -> Failed(ContinuationNotDurable). Builder::build runs it on every restart (over path) under the connection capability; result in Daemon::startup() (Cold | Resolved | Refused) and TaskTable::resolved(). No live TaskEntry is rebuilt. VolatileFact: TaskTable -> new Disposition::Resolved; ContinuationTable stays Declared, survives_as corrected to Some(Task) (the frontier is in the record, the pins are not). No IDL/schema/wire change. G1-08 pins flipped: store_shaped -> derived_scope_the_startup_pass_resolves_the_parked_task_from_the_store; AfterHandler test -> ..._reconnected_by_the_restart; new negative control (non-audit connection -> Startup::Refused) and a determinism test; g1_crash_recovery_evidence updated. just check: all green except dossier PLAN_BONE_TRACEABILITY staleness (lead-owned). RESUME-BRANCH DESIGN (not built, needs a new durable record shape): publish the continuation at park time as an ArtifactClass::Continuation record whose bytes are the cont_ preimage plus pins (snapshot, intent, PinnedEpochs, bounds, model source commitment, ledger ceilings), so the cont_ handle resolves in the store as task_ records do since bn-3dr. Needs publisher class scope to include Continuation (verification.rs publisher scope names Task only) and a decision on the workspace record (sealed snapshot is in store; the volatile workspace table is not). With that, resolve a bounded head whose cont_ record resolves and whose pins match current epochs to Resumable, otherwise Failed(ContinuationEpochMismatch-like typed reason). Open: task.status on a resolved handle still answers CapabilityDenied (a TaskRecord needs operation/epochs/budget/priority that were never durable); a re-issued verification.start after restart can mint a live entry under a handle that is already resolved Failed."}	blake3:RuwT_CF-r31_aQHJ4k6HjSevVbGFs8B4An3B8-83oKE
1790107623746445	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyoRA		item.create	bn-20142	{"description":"bn-1z09m built the plan §4.5 O2 startup task-resolution pass over durable task_ campaign records. It resolves every task through the Failed branch only: a bounded head answers Failed(ContinuationNotDurable) because the continuation's pins (epochs, bounds, intent, model source, budget ceilings) are not stored. Remaining debt: (1) publish the continuation durably as ArtifactClass::Continuation with its pins, widen the publisher's class scope, and let the startup pass resolve a bounded head to its committed continuation (the resume branch of O2); (2) task.status on a resolved handle answers CapabilityDenied because a wire TaskRecord needs operation, epochs, budget and priority, none of which are stored. New durable record format: check plan §4.4 artifact classes and RFC 0026 before choosing a shape; a new record class may be a schema change needing a typed compatibility statement. Pins: gate_g1_08_acceptance.rs module doc debt list.","kind":"task","labels":["req:g1-08"],"title":"durable continuation record: restart resume branch and task.status for resolved tasks (bn-1z09m)"}	blake3:_wecXWU7Vgz0liTGeN9a_S3iNxUY9qvM1AMw5QIqNog
1790107673630602	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyohA		item.comment	bn-2a7q9	{"body":"Follow-up from lead review: updated gate_g2_07_acceptance.rs's F3 doc lines (~84, ~144, ~157) to record the repair — the delivering suite now derives its privileged set from the IDL via its own idl_scan, and the intent.lock mutant now fails 2 delivering tests instead of 19/20 staying green. No assertions changed. cargo test -p continuumd --test gate_g2_07_acceptance: 27/27 pass. just check: only failure is dossier's PLAN_BONE_TRACEABILITY.md staleness (lead-owned exception per AGENTS.md); fmt/clippy/tests/boundaries all pass and just lean independently passes (19/19 jobs, axiom manifest up to date). Committed 352a59c: docs: record F3 repair in G2-07 acceptance (bn-2a7q9)."}	blake3:l1UN-Z1YWbV8f-bjMK7liMfejxVXo7TZJmx42XqPYpc
