1790108127546243	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyqxA		item.comment	bn-k99dt	{"body":"Fixed: StoreAudit::fsck now takes the declared identifier as an explicit argument instead of self.store.identifier. recovery::recover (continuumd) passes Blake3Identity explicitly; every other caller (15 files) passes the identifier its fixture already builds over. Flipped both pinned acceptance tests to regression guards: gate_g1_08_acceptance.rs's negative_control_a_substituted_identity_seam_is_caught_by_the_census_and_missed_by_fsck is renamed regression_a_substituted_identity_seam_is_caught_by_fsck_against_the_declared_seam and now asserts 3 IdentityMismatch defects; gate_g1_01_acceptance.rs's negative_control_a_non_blake3_seam_is_self_consistent_and_fails_this_files_predicate keeps its name (still accurate) and now asserts fsck(&Blake3Identity) flags every substituted entry. Also fixed g1_crash_recovery_evidence.rs's DriftingIdentity mutant control, which relied on fsck re-invoking the store's own identifier a second time at audit (no longer happens): it now derives real BLAKE3 while honest and a bogus hash from its first call when corrupt. just check: pass (fmt, clippy, all workspace tests, crate boundaries, dossier validator, lean build, axiom manifest)."}	blake3:0RS2fWPEjBfPyHlIF5ccqaunOeUozfr4vJngfHRq4dI
