1790139038151933	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEypBI		item.comment	bn-gzy1	{"body":"Committed 339b805 in WS. Reserve/commit/abort bound: tasks reserve checked obligation tokens (Transaction) via their own Cx; journal reserved -> committed|aborted from ObligationReserve/Commit/Abort trace; cancel-aborts placed canonically inside the holder's cancellation phases before its drain; holders write no suspend mark and yield once after a resolution. Lift: Reserve/Commit calculus steps, resolve-once, no leak at close; explicit abort is Inconclusive (no calculus step). Tests: tests/pr14_impl02_reserve_commit_abort.rs, 11 tests, 18,894 logs incl. sibling regions, 7 seeds, scripted differential, 3 projection identities, 5 mutation operators, typed refusals; 2 manual binding mutants killed. just check: all green except stale PLAN_BONE_TRACEABILITY (lead-owned); lean and test-policy pass."}	blake3:7806frbnAxpW-kZtF0s0BfLOkheXJB5106TZFa999as
1790139108830218	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEypRI		item.create	bn-15zfa	{"description":"bn-ybq's PR 15a exit map found a gap that no bone owns. continuum-model-core's Model holds only bounded integer variables and integer or boolean expressions. The replicated register's state is Map[Nat, Value], Map[Node, Map[Nat, Value]] and Set[Node], with option values, and its invariants quantify over whole types. Lowering refuses these as NonIntegerState, NonIntegerValue and Quantifier. epoch: Nat is unbounded, and ADR-0025 forbids bounding it silently. Deliver: extend the Model value domain and ModelBuilder with finite collection values, and finite quantifier expansion over declared finite sorts, under the bn-ybq output, depth and work budgets. Unbounded sorts need an explicit, typed bound from the run configuration (bn-3a9sr). Semantic-core change: GOV §4 record plus a dedicated security review. Blocks the PR-15A exit, bn-3qoo.","kind":"task","labels":["cml","phase-b","req:phase-b","req:pr-15a","req:phase-b-del-04"],"title":"Model value domain: collection-valued state (Map, Set, Option) and finite quantifier expansion for the replicated register (bn-ybq)"}	blake3:Ahg25-5Hok8lVmNvn3pDDN5kivIbOHdKJSqcuL9MHGM
1790139109049363	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyphI		item.create	bn-ujpz0	{"description":"bn-2270 observed C023 on the dependency graph and arrows A1/A2. Since bn-ybq, arrow A7 (asupersync adapter <-> executable primitive conformance models) has code on both sides: continuum-asupersync's lift into continuum_task, and continuum-model-core. But no cross-path test exists. Deliver: a test that checks the adapter's journals (PR-14 families) against an independently written executable conformance model, not the lift itself, with a mutant. Then record the witness in tools/triptych/evidence/c023.json, and widen the docs/18 C023 record to A7.","kind":"task","labels":["claim","req:phase-b","req:c023"],"title":"C023 arrow A7: cross-path test of the asupersync adapter journal against an executable conformance model (bn-2270)"}	blake3:J-LL1b6ZnKPsaYB8PzzXM3AyAtFDrmwO3GrhvcMqWxs
