1790142736731582	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy4RI		item.create	bn-3glnv	{"description":"bn-2ee4c landed library-level Ed25519 signing in continuum-evidence (ADR-0054): SigningRegistry, AllowedSigners, SignatureVerifier, and a fail-closed verify_for_ci_acceptance. Deliver: daemon operations and IDL/wire shapes to mint, rotate and revoke signer identities, attach and verify signatures on receipts, intent bundles and domain packs, and have intent.accept check a held bundle's chain with verify_for_ci_acceptance. Also distribute revocation records inside the intent bundle, and fix the schema example placeholders (ssh-ed25519: to ed25519:). Needs an RFC 0026/0037 revision. A protocol minor bump in Phase B needs the lead to confirm with the user before landing: bn-28kv4 was held for the 3.6 freeze, and the same question applies.","kind":"task","labels":["security","risk:high","req:phase-b"],"title":"Signing wiring: daemon operations and wire form for signatures and allowed-signers; intent.accept checks bundles with verify_for_ci_acceptance (bn-2ee4c)"}	blake3:UPLXj4TGi_Zl7iIjypN1Bz3A4VcW1GyzUvaQcbwcNrc
1790142736928269	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy4hI		item.create	bn-1hape	{"description":"bn-2ee4c's KeyEntropy is a capability with no production source (INV-005). Deliver: an OS entropy source in a boundary crate, never in continuum-evidence, behind the explicit capability; an on-disk keystore with the audited mint-on-first-use; and the producers of receipts, intent bundles and domain packs signing their canonical bytes through SigningRegistry::sign. Tests: keystore round trip, permissions, and no entropy reaching deterministic paths.","kind":"task","labels":["security","risk:high","req:phase-b"],"title":"Signing sources: an OS KeyEntropy capability in a boundary crate, an on-disk keystore, and signing inside the receipt, bundle and pack producers (bn-2ee4c)"}	blake3:rbB51g4NL_dra7P1criLPIKBb7iI9wdY6O1DNGY8MDE
