1790146148052723	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEygxM		item.comment	bn-2318t	{"body":"Done in ws bn-2318t, commit 52aa243. continuum-task only. Added WorkerStep::Abort, several staged publications per worker in slots (ReserveSlot/CommitSlot/AbortSlot, one obligation per slot, each resolved once), and a typed adapter-obligation entry point (RegionTree::open_substrate/discharge_substrate/transfer_substrate). Opens need a live holder in an open region and a new id. Discharges need a matching open by the live holder. Refusals are typed. is_total covers these obligations. Spec: RFC 0026 correction 51 plus a bullet under Atomicity of publication. Tests: continuum-task tests/region_abort_and_slots.rs (14) and region_substrate_ledger.rs (12). Differential against continuum-engine-reference in continuumd/tests/region_staging_differential.rs (69 states, 19 steps, mutant control). It lives in continuumd because a continuum-task -> engine-reference dev edge makes a cycle that the triptych acyclic rule rejects. Existing tests unchanged. GOV record tools/governance/reviews/bn-2318t.toml has no security table. just check: all pass except security-review-present (lead-owned; T09 review gates re-runs it). Follow-up: the continuum-asupersync lift must adopt Abort/slots/substrate ledger."}	blake3:mnLpm0LSVrhALgIwLxT6LxO_Vy-q7VsORBKFoJzdRBE
1790146184473974	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyhBM		item.create	bn-j1a50	{"description":"bn-2318t added WorkerStep::Abort, ReserveSlot/CommitSlot/AbortSlot (one publication per slot), and a public ledger entry (open_substrate, discharge_substrate, transfer_substrate) to continuum-task (RFC 0026 correction 51). Deliver in crates/continuum-asupersync: lift explicit ObligationToken::abort as Abort or AbortSlot (Conforms, not Unsupported); map each reservation to its own PublicationSlot, so tasks holding several tokens conform; move the obligations family's parallel ledger onto the substrate ledger, so is_total covers substrate obligations; update the pr14_impl02 pins (the_calculus_judges_real_runs_it_does_not_admit); and drop the reserve/commit/abort and obligations narrowings in START_HERE. Keep every journal byte and the A7 model agreement. Coordinate with bn-1i050, which edits the same lift.","kind":"task","labels":["phase-b","req:phase-b","req:pr-14"],"title":"PR-14 lift adopts the bn-2318t calculus APIs: explicit abort, per-reservation slots, and the substrate ledger inside is_total"}	blake3:QDL-ma6pO9seqlQTmyqSg_WRQX-q79x4TSNiYfjvMG0
