1790204619311787	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEynxQ		item.comment	bn-3il2r	{"body":"Updated PR-14 IMPL bullets in notes/plan/notes/START_HERE_IMPLEMENTATION.md (WS bn-3il2r, commit 0824f4d), verified against merged code/tests. Closed and removed: task/region lifecycle's is_total single-region-only narrowing (Finalization::ledger now subtree-scoped, RFC c53 item 5; region.rs is_total() reads the subtree ledger, region_task_cancellation.rs and pr14_deadline_cancellation.rs's child_finalizations>1000 check confirm) and obligations' 33-A7-perturbation narrowing (calculus decides cancellation per task at acknowledgement now, KNOWN_STRICTNESS=0 in a7_primitive_conformance.rs over 25,277 perturbations). Both got bn-36wy3 added to (delivered: ...). Virtual time's not-bound narrowing is closed (SpawnWithDeadline/CancelCause::Deadline bound, bn-36wy3 added to delivered, cited pr14_deadline_cancellation.rs: 7,572 logs, 242,304 projected journals, 34,944-run sample, 8 mutants, CancelRaced). Kept and restated: cancellation phases' multi-fault-ordering narrowing is untouched (unrelated to bn-36wy3). Added a new narrowing, owned by bn-28hup, on reserve/commit/abort and virtual time: EffectEvent::Reserved (effect.rs) checks no cancel phase and admits a reserve between a region's cancel request and the task's ack, but TimeEvent::Scheduled (time.rs) refuses a timer there via TimeFault::NotRunning once any phase is reported — confirmed by reading both lift functions. just traceability, just dossier (status: pass), and CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=8 just check (fmt/clippy/test/boundaries/covenant/governance/dossier/lean/test-policy) all pass."}	blake3:6aiLUz8xBn1686A-zzDgbg5PAwMKz6i8le6OXyNVmfI
