1790208246471626	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyshQ		item.comment	bn-2npu	{"body":"cr-10mg1y round 3 fixed. TCB-02 alias handling now fails closed by grammar: only type Name; or type Name = Path[<plain paths>]; is resolved; every other type item (generics, defaults, const generics, bounds, where), use-as renames of a verdict type and verdict-binding generic equalities fail as 'alias the scan cannot resolve' regardless of the inventory. Four new compiling fixtures (Decision<T = Verdict>, multi-hop via generic default, const-generic default, associated-type equality bound), each with its own inventory lines and exact diagnostic; 12 in total, all compile. Real checking base has no refused alias. Docs state TCB-02 is a conservative second line; the Rust entry-point tests are the authority. Lane unchanged (24/25; producer 4/7/1). just check green except lead-owned security-review-present, kernel-reviewers-present, T09 review gates."}	blake3:M14XqfuOVgqbVomoR9zu-bRzKyKRt_zq6wY9DzbJA90
