1790208354105323	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEytxQ		item.comment	bn-1ln12	{"body":"Done: commit 41bbb41. Model-core carries weak and strong fairness, each over a set of actions. The set is canonical and part of Model::identity, in an optional trailing section: fairness-free models keep their bytes, and a golden pins the new section. CML 'fairness s X' lowers to one assumption over the union of X's instances and candidates (a choice's actions too), never one per instance. cml.lower.fairness is withdrawn (RFC 0003 corr. 5, RFC 0008 note). The reference engine gains liveness (◇P, □◇P) with Emerson–Lei search, lasso witnesses, and an explicit Stuttering policy. The register lowers whole, and the configured.rs pin is now a regression guard. The register liveness verdicts equal an independent Kosaraju search: 6/6. The adversarial pass found 7 issues: 1 HIGH (a hidden progress assumption, fixed by the Stuttering policy) and 6 LOW (5 fixed, 1 noted). just check: green except security-review-present (lead-owned), which also fails check_t09 review gates. dossier, lean, and test-policy pass separately. PHASE-B-DEL-04 is not annotated, because it is PR 16's asupersync register."}	blake3:Ki6goxwSO2s6ao0QCSt70scp_mrJmq_t1WBuJHm4K7w
1790208399688638	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyuBQ		item.comment	bn-1ln12	{"body":"Lead rulings on the 41bbb41 report. (1) Model identity: I accept the optional trailing fairness section. It is additive, fairness-free models keep their continuum-model/1 bytes, and the goldens pin both cases. It is not a protocol major and moves no intent. (2) WF over a schema means the union of its instances. This is the weaker assumption, per RFC 0008/0015; per-instance fairness would be a privileged strengthening. (3) Explicit Stuttering with no default: accepted. The Codex security review follows."}	blake3:miKWh92FDy1cTJ_8SZt7P1BpKzKsgvbXiLpmLER9mMg
1790208401996417	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyuRQ		item.create	bn-rkrt7	{"description":"Since bn-1ln12 a Model carries weak and strong fairness assumptions. continuumd still labels every result's fairness as no-fairness-model. Report the model's real assumptions, and never claim a liveness result under fairness that the engine did not use.","kind":"task","labels":["phase-b","req:phase-b"],"title":"continuumd reports fairness: no-fairness-model for models that now carry fairness (bn-1ln12 follow-up)"}	blake3:2FbVGR5oFOGFeiWdf8omY3QRSVa6DxbMdzTOUtuue_4
