1790213447315395	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy2xQ		item.comment	bn-3glnv	{"body":"cr-2unxyh round 3 fixed at bec8be9.\n(1) RFC 0037 A1–A4. There is a new signed kind, intent-acceptance. Each chain element signs the canonical A1 statement (intent, base or genesis, capability, principal, time, previous element) under its own domain. Elements are verified in order, under local policy, and each signer must be active. A local accept at 3.8 is signed only for the admitted actor at the daemon's own time. The dummy tokens are gone. RFC 0037 correction 21 records this.\n(2) A receipt node keeps its exact first bytes and its first signature. stage never overwrites content under a colliding commitment.\n(3) Rotation links are applied as disjoint chains, so order does not matter. Permutation tests cover 2 and 3 hops.\n(4) ReceiptSigner::new refuses a registry that would leave an active key unrevocable (4096) or that exceeds the bound.\nTwo fresh-opus passes: the last one says mergeable. Residuals recorded in c21: a rotated acceptor needs a successor countersignature (follow-up), and relay needs the acceptor pinned.\njust check: only the lead-owned security-review-present failure remains."}	blake3:WHQ5c6o2sgkVHvab3wni2gm3zim_dUi3bAi07iwZ1Qc
1790213478720588	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy3BQ		item.create	bn-3rb3e	{"description":"bn-3glnv (RFC 0037 correction 21) chose the stricter reading: a rotated or revoked acceptor does not vouch, because no trusted time can date its signature before the rotation. So contracts accepted under a key that later rotates stop verifying. Add a successor countersignature over the prior acceptance chain, made at rotation, so that honest history survives rotation without trusting the retired key.","kind":"task","labels":["phase-b","req:phase-b","security","risk:high"],"title":"Intent acceptance: successor countersignature so contracts accepted under a later-rotated key keep vouching (bn-3glnv follow-up)"}	blake3:JbkNRZCpTVKXOsw41Cad9syE_IcYXHNjOMsaZBOiTSI
1790213478763161	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy3RQ		item.link	bn-3rb3e	{"link_type":"blocks","target":"bn-19p"}	blake3:-iHCnx5ewX4gJu0gswO7zBr6RPwKD1ElsHSwAggMZV4
1790214103729946	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy3hQ		item.comment	bn-eaxx0	{"body":"cr-19ec8g addressed in 4e49f53. obligation::finish's region loop returned at the first finalized-unsettled region regardless of its own balance, so a clean one scanned before a genuinely unbalanced one masked UnbalancedAtClose with Inconclusive. Same shape found three more places: obligation::finish's own leak-check loop preempting its region loop; cancellation::finish's two worker loops returning per-task; and lift()'s and_then chain of family finishes short-circuiting on the first Err, so lifecycle::finish's incomplete stopped effect/cancellation/obligation/time/channel finish from ever running. Fixed by deferring every Incomplete behind a flag until all checks that could find a violation have run, and running all six family finishes unconditionally in lift(), returning any violation immediately and only the first incomplete/unsupported once none is found. New tests: sibling_regions_one_clean_one_unbalanced_missing_settlement_is_unbalanced_at_close and nested_regions_..., each over both scan orders, verified to fail against the pre-cr-19ec8g code; two_regions_both_clean_missing_settlement_is_inconclusive is the control. A7 model agrees (judge_carried, boolean). RFC 0026 correction 57 added. just check: pass. Did not touch .seal, did not vote."}	blake3:5_ohzkeTrGp7BFKiIUGcbM8P9cs-7mwEjmRwiQ0U1gk
1790214187432362	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy3xQ		item.comment	bn-2npu	{"body":"cr-3i3rst round 7 handled per lead ruling. TCB-02 scoped to the forms it checks and documented as partial (trait-associated consts/types and unnamed forms not covered; complete check needs a rustc-derived public API). Completeness wording removed/scoped in tool docs, docs/18 C018 record, docs/18 C023 prose, kernel/certificate lib.rs docs and authority-test docs; no claims-baseline row moved. New pinned known-miss fixture tcb02-trait-associated-const: compiles, accepted by the scan and the core authority test, recorded in evidence tcb02_known_misses. Everything else kept. Lane 24/25; producer 4/7/1; 23 fixtures. just check green except lead-owned security-review-present, kernel-reviewers-present, T09 review gates."}	blake3:Gk0PnNE_NlCAEAA9qLN3xokjG96YBlQGYvBsRazOwRw
1790214518555258	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy4BQ		item.comment	bn-33g98	{"body":"TEST-3-08 flipped to enforced. Added crates/continuum-cml-elab/tests/guard_equivalence.rs (3 tests: nested-conjunction split equals 3 separate requires incl. lowered Model identity; negative control for a dropped conjunct / changed bound; mutant disabling conjunct-splitting via a hand-built NormModel, showing the identity breaks). Bound in tools/test-policy/sections/s3_metamorphic_relations_07_10.py via RUST_BINDING (existence/#[test]/not-ignored/assertion-token checks, same discipline as TEST-3-07/09), with fixtures 08_rust_binding_missing.json and clean_rust_binding_3_08.json. No drift check needed: the tsys-level De Morgan/double-negation check is not a port of elab.rs's algorithm (same as TEST-3-09/CVNF-1). Only rules norm.rs/RFC 0003 actually implement are tested; no general commutative &&/|| rewrite, double-negation, or comparison-flip exists outside the unrelated recursion measure_test heuristic. docs/19 §3 annotated (delivered: bn-33g98), just traceability run, evidence regenerated. just check: pass (fmt, clippy, tests, dossier, lean, test-policy, differential corpus). HEAD 20be496 in workspace, not merged."}	blake3:2Fzjlx5qG9nMhhDgHedGJs8U_nr7C9PHRGhjixPnb2I
